IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb4-common`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part XVIII, ss 221 to 225: THE LIQUIDATOR AND
-- THE END OF A LIQUIDATION.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. What a liquidator must do (s 221) and may do (s 222), the year in which the final
-- accounts must be put to the court (s 223), a shareholder's right to a distribution in money (s 224), and
-- the duty to keep the records for the prescribed period, with its offence (s 225).
--
-- "Forthwith" (ss 221(a), 223(6)) and "without delay" (s 221(b)) are not converted to days: the duty arises
-- on the event and no day count is invented. Section 155 (financial statements), section 262 (certificate)
-- and the "prescribed period" of s 225(1) (regulations) are not among the sources.
--
-- "Within one year after appointment" (s 223(2)) and "not later than two months after the first
-- publication" (s 221(b)(iii)) are counted by the keel: the appointment (or publication) day is day 0, and
-- the last day is the same day one year (or two months) on (keel fork F1).

§§ `s 221 Duties of the liquidator`

-- src:2763 | Duties of liquidator
-- src:2764 | 221 A liquidator shall
-- src:2765 | (a) forthwith after appointment give notice thereof to the Director and to each claimant and creditor known to the liquidator;
@ref CBCA s 221(a) (src:2765)
GIVEN `the liquidator has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must give notice of the appointment to the Director and each known claimant and creditor within s 221(a)` MEANS
    `the liquidator has been appointed`

@ref CBCA s 221(a) (src:2765)
GIVEN `the notice was given to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given to each claimant and creditor known to the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator's notice of the appointment is complete within s 221(a)` MEANS
        `the notice was given to the Director`
    AND `the notice was given to each claimant and creditor known to the liquidator`

-- src:2766 | (b) without delay publish notice by insertion once a week for two consecutive weeks in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office and take reasonable steps to give notice of the appointment in each province where the corporation carries on business, requiring any person
-- src:2767 | (i) indebted to the corporation, to render an account and pay to the liquidator at the time and place specified any amount owing,
-- src:2768 | (ii) possessing property of the corporation, to deliver it to the liquidator at the time and place specified, and
-- src:2769 | (iii) having a claim against the corporation, whether liquidated, unliquidated, future or contingent, to present particulars thereof in writing to the liquidator not later than two months after the first publication of the notice;
@ref CBCA s 221(b) (src:2766)
GIVEN `the liquidator has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must publish and give notice of the appointment within s 221(b)` MEANS
    `the liquidator has been appointed`

@ref CBCA s 221(b) (src:2766)
GIVEN `the notice was published once a week for two consecutive weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable steps were taken to give notice in each province where the corporation carries on business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator's publication and notice are complete within s 221(b)` MEANS
        `the notice was published once a week for two consecutive weeks`
    AND `it was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office`
    AND `reasonable steps were taken to give notice in each province where the corporation carries on business`

@ref CBCA s 221(b)(i) (src:2767)
GIVEN `the person is indebted to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person indebted to the corporation is required to render an account and pay within s 221(b)(i)` MEANS
    `the person is indebted to the corporation`

@ref CBCA s 221(b)(ii) (src:2768)
GIVEN `the person possesses property of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person possessing property of the corporation is required to deliver it within s 221(b)(ii)` MEANS
    `the person possesses property of the corporation`

@ref CBCA s 221(b)(iii) (src:2769)
GIVEN `the person has a claim against the corporation, whether liquidated, unliquidated, future or contingent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person with a claim is required to present particulars in writing within s 221(b)(iii)` MEANS
    `the person has a claim against the corporation, whether liquidated, unliquidated, future or contingent`

@ref CBCA s 221(b)(iii) (src:2769)
GIVEN `the day the notice was first published` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a person with a claim to present particulars within s 221(b)(iii)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) `counted from` `the day the notice was first published`

@ref CBCA s 221(b)(iii) (src:2769)
GIVEN `the day the notice was first published` IS A DATE
      `the day the particulars were presented` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the particulars were presented in time within s 221(b)(iii)` MEANS
    `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) `the day the notice was first published` `the day the particulars were presented`

-- src:2770 | (c) take into custody and control the property of the corporation;
-- src:2771 | (d) open and maintain a trust account for the moneys of the corporation;
-- src:2772 | (e) keep accounts of the moneys of the corporation received and paid out by the liquidator;
-- src:2773 | (f) maintain separate lists of the shareholders, creditors and other persons having claims against the corporation;
-- src:2774 | (g) if at any time the liquidator determines that the corporation is unable to pay or adequately provide for the discharge of its obligations, apply to the court for directions;
-- src:2775 | (h) deliver to the court and to the Director, at least once in every twelve month period after appointment or more often as the court may require, financial statements of the corporation in the form required by section 155 or in such other form as the liquidator may think proper or as the court may require; and
-- src:2776 | (i) after the final accounts are approved by the court, distribute any remaining property of the corporation among the shareholders according to their respective rights.
@ref CBCA s 221(c) (src:2770)
GIVEN `the liquidator has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must take into custody and control the property of the corporation within s 221(c)` MEANS
    `the liquidator has been appointed`

@ref CBCA s 221(d) (src:2771)
GIVEN `the liquidator has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must open and maintain a trust account for the moneys of the corporation within s 221(d)` MEANS
    `the liquidator has been appointed`

@ref CBCA s 221(e) (src:2772)
GIVEN `the liquidator has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must keep accounts of the moneys received and paid out within s 221(e)` MEANS
    `the liquidator has been appointed`

@ref CBCA s 221(f) (src:2773)
GIVEN `the liquidator has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must maintain separate lists of shareholders, creditors and other claimants within s 221(f)` MEANS
    `the liquidator has been appointed`

@ref CBCA s 221(g) (src:2774)
GIVEN `the liquidator determines that the corporation is unable to pay or adequately provide for the discharge of its obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must apply to the court for directions within s 221(g)` MEANS
    `the liquidator determines that the corporation is unable to pay or adequately provide for the discharge of its obligations`

-- (h): "at least once in every twelve month period after appointment": the first period runs from the
-- appointment; the next from the end of the first (and so on). Delivered to the court AND the Director.
@ref CBCA s 221(h) (src:2775)
GIVEN `the start of the twelve month period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the financial statements for a twelve month period within s 221(h)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 12, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) `counted from` `the start of the twelve month period`

@ref CBCA s 221(h) (src:2775)
GIVEN `the start of the twelve month period` IS A DATE
      `the day the financial statements were delivered to the court` IS A DATE
      `the day the financial statements were delivered to the Director` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the financial statements were delivered in time within s 221(h)` MEANS
        `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 12, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) `the start of the twelve month period` `the day the financial statements were delivered to the court`
    AND `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 12, `unit of time` IS `calendar months`) `the start of the twelve month period` `the day the financial statements were delivered to the Director`

-- The form: s 155's, or another form the liquidator thinks proper, or one the court requires. Read as written
-- (fork F6), the three are alternatives, so a form the liquidator thinks proper is enough.
@ref CBCA s 221(h) (src:2775)
GIVEN `the statements are in the form required by section 155` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements are in another form the liquidator thinks proper` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements are in the form the court requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the form of the financial statements is acceptable within s 221(h)` MEANS
        `the statements are in the form required by section 155`
    OR  `the statements are in another form the liquidator thinks proper`
    OR  `the statements are in the form the court requires`

@ref CBCA s 221(i) (src:2776)
GIVEN `the court has approved the final accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must distribute the remaining property among the shareholders within s 221(i)` MEANS
    `the court has approved the final accounts`

§§ `s 222 Powers of the liquidator`

-- src:2777 | Powers of liquidator
-- src:2778 | 222 (1) A liquidator may
-- src:2779 | (a) retain lawyers, accountants, engineers, appraisers and other professional advisers;
-- src:2780 | (b) bring, defend or take part in any civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding in the name and on behalf of the corporation;
-- src:2781 | (c) carry on the business of the corporation as required for an orderly liquidation;
-- src:2782 | (d) sell by public auction or private sale any property of the corporation;
-- src:2783 | (e) do all acts and execute or, in Quebec, sign any documents in the name and on behalf of the corporation;
-- src:2784 | (f) borrow money on the security of the property of the corporation;
-- src:2785 | (g) settle or compromise any claims by or against the corporation; and
-- src:2786 | (h) do all other things necessary for the liquidation of the corporation and distribution of its property.
@ref CBCA s 222(1) (src:2778-2786)
DECLARE `Kind of act under s 222(1)` IS ONE OF
    `retain lawyers, accountants, engineers, appraisers and other professional advisers (s 222(1)(a))`
    `bring, defend or take part in any civil, criminal or administrative action or proceeding in the name and on behalf of the corporation (s 222(1)(b))`
    `carry on the business of the corporation (s 222(1)(c))`
    `sell any property of the corporation by public auction or private sale (s 222(1)(d))`
    `do all acts and execute or, in Quebec, sign any documents in the name and on behalf of the corporation (s 222(1)(e))`
    `borrow money on the security of the property of the corporation (s 222(1)(f))`
    `settle or compromise any claims by or against the corporation (s 222(1)(g))`
    `do another thing necessary for the liquidation and distribution of the property (s 222(1)(h))`
    `an act the section does not list`

@ref CBCA s 222(1) (src:2778-2786)
GIVEN act IS A `Kind of act under s 222(1)`
      `the business is required for an orderly liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is necessary for the liquidation of the corporation and the distribution of its property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`whether a liquidator may do the act within s 222(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `carry on the business of the corporation (s 222(1)(c))` THEN (IF `the business is required for an orderly liquidation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    WHEN `do another thing necessary for the liquidation and distribution of the property (s 222(1)(h))` THEN (IF `the thing is necessary for the liquidation of the corporation and the distribution of its property` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    WHEN `an act the section does not list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2787 | Due diligence
-- src:2788 | (2) A liquidator is not liable if the liquidator exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances, including reliance in good faith on
-- src:2789 | (a) financial statements of the corporation represented to the liquidator by an officer of the corporation or in a written report of the auditor of the corporation fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation; or
-- src:2790 | (b) a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by the professional person.
@ref CBCA s 222(2) (src:2788-2790)
GIVEN `the liquidator exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liquidator relied in good faith on financial statements represented by an officer, or on a written report of the auditor, fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liquidator relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator is not liable within s 222(2)` MEANS
        `the liquidator exercised the care, diligence and skill that a reasonably prudent person would have exercised in comparable circumstances`
    OR  `the liquidator relied in good faith on financial statements represented by an officer, or on a written report of the auditor, fairly to reflect the financial condition of the corporation`
    OR  `the liquidator relied in good faith on a report of a person whose profession lends credibility to a statement made by that person`

-- src:2791 | Application for examination
-- src:2792 | (3) If a liquidator has reason to believe that any person has in their possession or under their control, or has concealed, withheld or misappropriated any property of the corporation, the liquidator may apply to the court for an order requiring that person to appear before the court at the time and place designated in the order and to be examined.
@ref CBCA s 222(3) (src:2792)
GIVEN `the liquidator has reason to believe that a person has in their possession or under their control, or has concealed, withheld or misappropriated, any property of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator may apply for an order that the person appear and be examined within s 222(3)` MEANS
    `the liquidator has reason to believe that a person has in their possession or under their control, or has concealed, withheld or misappropriated, any property of the corporation`

-- src:2793 | Power of court
-- src:2794 | (4) If the examination referred to in subsection (3) discloses that a person has concealed, withheld or misappropriated property of the corporation, the court may order that person to restore it or pay compensation to the liquidator.
@ref CBCA s 222(4) (src:2794)
GIVEN `the examination discloses that the person concealed, withheld or misappropriated property of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may order the person to restore the property or pay compensation to the liquidator within s 222(4)` MEANS
    `the examination discloses that the person concealed, withheld or misappropriated property of the corporation`

§§ `s 223 Costs, final accounts, final order`

-- src:2795 | Costs of liquidation
-- src:2796 | 223 (1) A liquidator shall pay the costs of liquidation out of the property of the corporation and shall pay or make adequate provision for all claims against the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 223(1) (src:2796)
GIVEN `the liquidator has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must pay the costs of liquidation and pay or provide for all claims within s 223(1)` MEANS
    `the liquidator has been appointed`

-- (2): one year after appointment; the duty arises once the claims are paid or provided for.
-- src:2797 | Final accounts
-- src:2798 | (2) Within one year after appointment, and after paying or making adequate provision for all claims against the corporation, the liquidator shall apply to the court
-- src:2799 | (a) for approval of the final accounts and for an order permitting the liquidator to distribute in money or in kind the remaining property of the corporation to its shareholders according to their respective rights; or
-- src:2800 | (b) for an extension of time, setting out the reasons therefor.
@ref CBCA s 223(2) (src:2798-2800)
GIVEN `the day the liquidator was appointed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the liquidator's application to the court within s 223(2)` MEANS
    `the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 1, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` `the day the liquidator was appointed`

@ref CBCA s 223(2) (src:2798)
GIVEN `the liquidator has paid or made adequate provision for all claims against the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must apply to the court within s 223(2)` MEANS
    `the liquidator has paid or made adequate provision for all claims against the corporation`

@ref CBCA s 223(2)(a), (b) (src:2799-2800)
DECLARE `Kind of application under s 223(2)` IS ONE OF
    `for approval of the final accounts and an order permitting distribution of the remaining property to the shareholders (s 223(2)(a))`
    `for an extension of time, setting out the reasons (s 223(2)(b))`
    `an application of another kind`

@ref CBCA s 223(2) (src:2798-2800)
GIVEN `the day the liquidator was appointed` IS A DATE
      `the day the liquidator applied` IS A DATE
      application IS A `Kind of application under s 223(2)`
      `the application sets out the reasons for the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator's application satisfies s 223(2)` MEANS
        `done within the time limit` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 1, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `the day the liquidator was appointed` `the day the liquidator applied`
    AND (CONSIDER application
         WHEN `for approval of the final accounts and an order permitting distribution of the remaining property to the shareholders (s 223(2)(a))` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `for an extension of time, setting out the reasons (s 223(2)(b))` THEN `the application sets out the reasons for the extension`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- src:2801 | Shareholder application
-- src:2802 | (3) If a liquidator fails to make the application required by subsection (2), a shareholder of the corporation may apply to the court for an order for the liquidator to show cause why a final accounting and distribution should not be made.
@ref CBCA s 223(3) (src:2802)
GIVEN `the person is a shareholder of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liquidator has failed to make the application required by subsection 223(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a shareholder may apply for an order that the liquidator show cause within s 223(3)` MEANS
        `the person is a shareholder of the corporation`
    AND `the liquidator has failed to make the application required by subsection 223(2)`

-- src:2803 | Publication
-- src:2804 | (4) A liquidator shall give notice of their intention to make an application under subsection (2) to the Director, to each inspector appointed under section 217, to each shareholder and to any person who provided a security, fidelity bond or fidelity insurance for the liquidation, and shall publish the notice in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office, or as otherwise directed by the court.
@ref CBCA s 223(4) (src:2804)
GIVEN `notice of the intention to apply was given to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was given to each inspector appointed under section 217` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was given to each shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `notice was given to each person who provided a security, fidelity bond or fidelity insurance for the liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office, or as otherwise directed by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator's notice of intention to apply complies with s 223(4)` MEANS
        `notice of the intention to apply was given to the Director`
    AND `notice was given to each inspector appointed under section 217`
    AND `notice was given to each shareholder`
    AND `notice was given to each person who provided a security, fidelity bond or fidelity insurance for the liquidation`
    AND `the notice was published in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office, or as otherwise directed by the court`

-- src:2805 | Final order
-- src:2806 | (5) If the court approves the final accounts rendered by a liquidator, the court shall make an order
-- src:2807 | (a) directing the Director to issue a certificate of dissolution;
-- src:2808 | (b) directing the custody or disposal of the documents and records of the corporation; and
-- src:2809 | (c) subject to subsection (6), discharging the liquidator.
@ref CBCA s 223(5)(a) (src:2806-2807)
GIVEN `the court has approved the final accounts rendered by the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court must order the Director to issue a certificate of dissolution within s 223(5)(a)` MEANS
    `the court has approved the final accounts rendered by the liquidator`

@ref CBCA s 223(5)(b) (src:2806 src:2808)
GIVEN `the court has approved the final accounts rendered by the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court must order the custody or disposal of the documents and records within s 223(5)(b)` MEANS
    `the court has approved the final accounts rendered by the liquidator`

-- (c) "subject to subsection (6)": (6) is a duty that arises only once the order exists, so it cannot be a
-- precondition of the order that discharges the liquidator. Read as: the discharge does not release the
-- liquidator from (6).
@ref CBCA s 223(5)(c) (src:2806 src:2809)
GIVEN `the court has approved the final accounts rendered by the liquidator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court must order the liquidator's discharge within s 223(5)(c)` MEANS
    `the court has approved the final accounts rendered by the liquidator`

-- src:2810 | Delivery of order
-- src:2811 | (6) The liquidator shall forthwith send a certified copy of the order referred to in subsection (5) to the Director.
@ref CBCA s 223(6) (src:2811)
GIVEN `the court has made the order referred to in subsection 223(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liquidator must send a certified copy of the order to the Director within s 223(6)` MEANS
    `the court has made the order referred to in subsection 223(5)`

-- src:2812 | Certificate of dissolution
-- src:2813 | (7) On receipt of the order referred to in subsection (5), the Director shall issue a certificate of dissolution in accordance with section 262.
@ref CBCA s 223(7) (src:2813)
GIVEN `the Director has received the order referred to in subsection 223(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director must issue a certificate of dissolution within s 223(7)` MEANS
    `the Director has received the order referred to in subsection 223(5)`

-- src:2814 | Effect of certificate
-- src:2815 | (8) The corporation ceases to exist on the date shown in the certificate of dissolution.
@ref CBCA s 223(8) (src:2815)
GIVEN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation exists on a day within s 223(8)` MEANS
    `the day asked about` LESS THAN `the date shown in the certificate of dissolution`

§§ `s 224 Right to distribution in money`

-- src:2816 | Right to distribution in money
-- src:2817 | 224 (1) If in the course of liquidation of a corporation the shareholders resolve or the liquidator proposes to
-- src:2818 | (a) exchange all or substantially all the property of the corporation for securities of another body corporate that are to be distributed to the shareholders, or
-- src:2819 | (b) distribute all or part of the property of the corporation to the shareholders in kind,
-- src:2820 | a shareholder may apply to the court for an order requiring the distribution of the property of the corporation to be in money.
@ref CBCA s 224(1) (src:2817-2820)
GIVEN `the shareholders resolve or the liquidator proposes to exchange all or substantially all the property of the corporation for securities of another body corporate to be distributed to the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholders resolve or the liquidator proposes to distribute all or part of the property of the corporation to the shareholders in kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal is made in the course of liquidation of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a shareholder may apply to the court for a distribution in money within s 224(1)` MEANS
        `the proposal is made in the course of liquidation of the corporation`
    AND (    `the shareholders resolve or the liquidator proposes to exchange all or substantially all the property of the corporation for securities of another body corporate to be distributed to the shareholders`
         OR  `the shareholders resolve or the liquidator proposes to distribute all or part of the property of the corporation to the shareholders in kind`)

-- src:2821 | Powers of court
-- src:2822 | (2) On an application under subsection (1), the court may order
-- src:2823 | (a) all the property of the corporation to be converted into and distributed in money; or
-- src:2824 | (b) the claims of any shareholder applying under this section to be satisfied by a distribution in money, in which case subsections 190(20) to (22) apply.
@ref CBCA s 224(2) (src:2822-2824)
DECLARE `Kind of order under s 224(2)` IS ONE OF
    `an order that all the property of the corporation be converted into and distributed in money (s 224(2)(a))`
    `an order that the claims of the applying shareholder be satisfied by a distribution in money (s 224(2)(b))`
    `an order of another kind than those s 224(2) names`

@ref CBCA s 224(2) (src:2822-2824)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection 224(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `Kind of order under s 224(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make the order within s 224(2)` MEANS
        `an application has been made under subsection 224(1)`
    AND (CONSIDER order
         WHEN `an order of another kind than those s 224(2) names` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)

@ref CBCA s 224(2)(b) (src:2824)
GIVEN order IS A `Kind of order under s 224(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`subsections 190(20) to (22) apply within s 224(2)(b)` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `an order that the claims of the applying shareholder be satisfied by a distribution in money (s 224(2)(b))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 225 Custody of documents; offence`

-- src:2825 | Custody of documents
-- src:2826 | 225 (1) A person who has been granted custody of the documents and records of a dissolved corporation remains liable to produce those documents and records until the end of the prescribed period or of any shorter period fixed by an order made under subsection 223(5).
@ref CBCA s 225(1) (src:2826)
GIVEN `the end of the prescribed period` IS A DATE
      `the end of a shorter period fixed by an order made under subsection 223(5)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the custodian remains liable to produce the documents and records within s 225(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the end of a shorter period fixed by an order made under subsection 223(5)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the end of the prescribed period`
    WHEN JUST shorter THEN `the earlier of two dates` shorter `the end of the prescribed period`

@ref CBCA s 225(1) (src:2826)
GIVEN `the person has been granted custody of the documents and records of a dissolved corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day the person remains liable` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the custodian remains liable to produce the documents and records on a day within s 225(1)` MEANS
        `the person has been granted custody of the documents and records of a dissolved corporation`
    AND `the day asked about` AT MOST `the last day the person remains liable`

-- src:2827 | Offence
-- src:2828 | (2) A person who, without reasonable cause, contravenes subsection (1) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 225(2) (src:2828)
GIVEN `the person remains liable under subsection 225(1) and has not produced the documents and records` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the custodian is guilty of an offence within s 225(2)` MEANS
        `the person remains liable under subsection 225(1) and has not produced the documents and records`
    AND (NOT `the person has reasonable cause`)

@ref CBCA s 225(2) (src:2828)
GIVEN `the fine in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the penalty is within the limits of s 225(2)` MEANS
        `the fine in dollars` AT MOST 5000
    AND `the months of imprisonment` AT MOST 6
